For all those of you who have been waiting for the latest revision of the
Wheaton College Nethack Spoiler File, here's the latest scoop:

Remember how I said that a revision would be coming out around Christmas
time?  Well - I lied.  Several factors have necessitated the postponement
of releasing the latest revision until January 12.  Among these is the
fact (as pointed out by a friend) that a lot of you nethack fans will be
gone during the days immediately around Christmas, and the spoilers would
get expired, and then I'd get tons of requests for a re-post.

Sooo... I will be posting the latest revision on January 12.  Be looking
for it soon thereafter.  Here's what will be included:

   - As always, many small details have been modified and/or corrected.
   - An all new section on common questions and their answers has been
     added, covering stuff like how to get rid of an iron ball and how
     to get your character back after changing the name due to a 
     polymorph (what say we post this automatically ever day?).    :-)
   - A section has been added that details formulae for how much you
     can carry.
   - The artifacts secton has been moved to right after the weapons
     section in order to prevent confusion and tie in with two new
     sections...
   - A section has been added that details exactly how the game computes
     whether or not you hit a monster
   - And... a section has been added which will allow you to figure out
     exactly how much damage your weapons can do
   - A new section has been added on "nethack abuse" - or how to take
     advantage of parts of the game, such as polypiling, sink/black
     pudding abuse, the troll dance of death, cursed scrolls of genocide,
     etc.
   - A *HUGE* new section has been added on monsters, detailing levels,
     attacks, experience points, resistances, etc.

So... Be on the lookout around about January 12!

